[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles UCSI Software Requirements Specification
UID: DHF-HRC-UCSI-0001
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-ucsi

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the software requirements for the Heracles UCSI service interface.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
UCSI is a technician-facing service interface for the Heracles superficial radiation therapy system. It is available as a standalone application and as a module hosted by the system PC software. It presents system telemetry, status, and servicing information and provides manual high-voltage power supply (HVPS) control for service activities, including manually initiated X-ray emission.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
===================  ==========================================
Abbreviation/Term    Definition
===================  ==========================================
HVPS                 High Voltage Power Supply
SDS                  Software Design Specification
SRS                  Software Requirements Specification
UCSI                 Heracles technician-facing service interface
===================  ==========================================
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-UCSI-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-001
TYPE: Interface
TITLE: Deployment modes
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall provide the UCSI service interface when operated as a standalone application and when hosted by the system PC software.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-002
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: System telemetry and status
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to view current system operating parameters, communication status, system status, interlock status, active faults, and operational logs, and to save the displayed logs to a file.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-003
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Telemetry monitoring and session data
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to select system operating parameters for numerical monitoring and graphical display of their telemetry history. The software shall record live telemetry sessions, load recorded sessions for play, pause, and timeline seeking, return from replay to live monitoring, and preserve recent live telemetry in CSV exports requested by the operator or created automatically for fault diagnosis.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-004
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Manual HVPS service control
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to command HVPS operating parameters and to enable and disable manual X-ray emission for service activities. The software shall display the associated HVPS feedback and interlock status to the operator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-005
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Coil service control
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to command coil operating parameters for service activities and to view the associated coil feedback values.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-006
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Control system configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall allow the operator to view and set control system configuration values for service activities.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-007
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Version information
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall display version information for the GCB firmware, HVPS firmware, and CNC software.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-008
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Standalone fault clearing
STATEMENT: >>>
The standalone UCSI application shall allow the operator to clear active system faults. The clear-faults command shall be unavailable when UCSI is hosted by the system PC software.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-009
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: HVPS fault-status display
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall display the HVPS fault statuses reported by system telemetry.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-UCSI-010
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Telemetry-gated service and one-point test emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall maintain communication with the GCB and shall transmit operator-issued
service commands only when current live telemetry reports a control state that permits the
requested action. The software shall prevent those commands during telemetry replay and
when live telemetry is missing or stale.

The software shall allow a qualified operator to run and stop a one-point X-ray test
emission using parameters within the configured service limits. The command sequence shall
advance only after current live telemetry confirms each required control-state transition.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
